## Overview

**misocialr** reads the
[MI Social API](https://aplicacoes.mds.gov.br/sagi/servicos/misocial) of the
Brazilian Ministry of Development and Social Assistance (MDS/SAGI): monthly
values for every municipality, from the Cadastro Unico, the Bolsa Familia
programme, the BPC benefit, the social assistance network and its funding,
Bolsa Familia conditionalities and food security programmes.

Every retrieval function returns a long tibble with one row per field x
municipality x month in which the API has a value.

```{r}
library(misocialr)
```

## Themes and fields

The package ships a curated dictionary. Each theme has a shortcut function.

```{r}
mds_themes()
```

```{r}
mds_fields("bpc_suas")
```

The API has no data dictionary of its own: labels are a reading of the
technical names, checked against the published values. Any other field can be
requested by name in `mds_data()`; `mds_api_fields()` lists what the API
publishes for one municipality.

## Retrieving data

Periods are months (`YYYYMM`), years, or `-n` for the last *n* months.
Localities are `"BR"`, states (`"PE"` or `26`) or IBGE municipality codes
with 6 or 7 digits, in any combination.

```{r}
recife <- mds_bolsa_familia(
  periods = c(202508, 202509),
  localities = 2611606,
  fields = c("qtd_familias_beneficiarias_bolsa_familia_i",
             "valor_repassado_bolsa_familia_f")
)
recife[, c("ibge_code", "period", "field", "value")]
```

The API identifies municipalities by the first six digits of the IBGE code;
`ibge_code7()` restores the official code, including the nine municipalities
whose code does not follow the check-digit rule.

```{r}
ibge_code7(c("261160", "261153"))
```

## Months not published yet

The API answers `0`, not "missing", for months that were not published.
`mds_periods()` counts, per month, the municipalities with a value and those
with a non-zero value:

```{r}
tail(mds_periods("bpc_ben_i", localities = "PE"), 5)
```

`mds_data()` returns the values as published. `mds_drop_unpublished()`
removes future months and trailing months in which every returned locality
is zero, and says what it removed:

```{r}
bpc <- mds_bpc_suas(periods = 2026, localities = "PE", fields = "bpc_ben_i")
range(bpc$period)
```

```{r, message = TRUE}
bpc <- mds_drop_unpublished(bpc)
range(bpc$period)
```

## Checks behind the labels

Where fields are parts of a total, the parts were summed against the total
before labelling. For example, the Cadastro Unico income brackets are
disjoint:

```{r}
cad <- mds_cadunico(
  periods = 202508, localities = "BR",
  fields = c("cadun_qtd_familias_cadastradas_pobreza_pbf_i",
             "cadun_qtd_familias_cadastradas_baixa_renda_i",
             "cadun_qtd_familias_cadastradas_rfpc_ate_meio_sm_i")
)
totals <- tapply(cad$value, cad$field, sum)
totals
totals[["cadun_qtd_familias_cadastradas_pobreza_pbf_i"]] +
  totals[["cadun_qtd_familias_cadastradas_baixa_renda_i"]] ==
  totals[["cadun_qtd_familias_cadastradas_rfpc_ate_meio_sm_i"]]
```

so "baixa renda" is the bracket between the poverty line and half a minimum
wage. The other checks are listed in the package README.

```{r, echo = FALSE}
cat("Built on", format(Sys.Date()), "against the live API.\n")
```
